# tap_to_move · tap the floor and the player walks there by themselves; the stick still works and takes over
# tap_to_move(reach, speed) makes the scene a game and, on a tap, walks the player to the point tapped when it is
# within `reach` metres (30) and no higher than half a metre above their feet (a floor, a step, a low seat's top,
# not a wall or a shelf). `speed` 0 walks at the scene's walking speed. Pairs with walk_controls.
# kind: script
# place: tap_to_move()
# credit: J Production, made in Loop3D
# licence: our own work, free for every J Production project
# from: the library's Scripts shelf (2026-11-23)
# tags: controls, tap, click to move, point and click, touch, walk, game, script
to tap_to_move(reach: 30, speed: 0)
  mode "game"
  when "tap"
    if event.hit and event.distance < reach and event.at.y < player().y + 0.5
      walk_player(event.at, speed: speed)
